    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Cal Raleigh** (78.02) and **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) headline the lineup as our most efficient starters. **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Jeffrey Springs, where his power profile aligns perfectly with a favorable park factor and a soft SP_xERA of 4.84. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** is our standout OF play; his strong platoon advantage against George Kirby, combined with his dual-threat potential, makes him a primary target for points. **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) also warrants attention, as he faces a struggling Max Scherzer (5.10 xERA). His leadoff positioning, coupled with a rare \"slow delivery\" flag on the mound, grants him an elite stolen base environment that significantly inflates his score above his base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Yainer Diaz** (41.14) on the bench. Despite his high base projection, the matchup against Rasmussen (3.27 xERA) proved too daunting to justify starting him over more favorable platoon splits in the UTIL and C slots. **Yainer Diaz** fell just short of the required threshold as the optimizer prioritized the stolen base upside of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.58) and the platoon leverage provided by **Kyle Karros** (60.59). **Kyle Karros** specifically benefited from a +7% boost due to his platoon edge against Valdez and an favorable environment for base-running, pushing his score comfortably into the \"Strong\" category.\n\nRisk management remains a theme for today, particularly with **Bryce Harper** (49.40) and **Daulton Varsho** (45.29). Both players are tethered to sub-3.30 xERA pitchers\u2014Chris Sale and Rasmussen, respectively\u2014which suppressed their efficiency despite their talent. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, **Zack Gelof**, **Alex Freeland**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Lawrence Butler**. Should their official batting positions drift downward in the lineup, their efficiency scores will require re-evaluation before the first pitch. No major weather concerns have been flagged, but we will continue to watch for late-breaking wind shifts that could impact **Jung Hoo Lee**, who is currently benefiting from a +5% wind-out adjustment.",
